# VTID-03764 — commands run this session

## Root-cause investigation (before this diagnostic instrumentation)

Real Playwright measurements against https://preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com
(staging, commit 65772496 = VTID-03741 merged), authenticated as the
documented test user a27552a3-0257-4305-8ed0-351a80fd3701, using the real
orb-widget.js VitanaOrb.toggle() path (same code a FAB tap runs). 20 real
sessions total across two batches (rapid-fire, then 90s-spaced to rule out
self-induced contention). Cross-referenced against real
oasis_events.voice.latency.measured rows (Supabase project
inmkhvwdcuyhnxkgfvsb) for exact server-side phase timing.

Findings, in order ruled out:
1. Hypothesis "rapid back-to-back testing causes throttling" — DISPROVEN.
   Spaced-out sessions (90s apart) show the identical bimodal pattern.
2. Hypothesis "large context (27502 chars) makes Nova slower" — DISPROVEN
   as a full explanation. Both context_chars=0 and context_chars=27500+
   groups show the same huge variance (2-13s) independently.
3. Hypothesis "Nova connection error triggers a slow retry" — DISPROVEN.
   Zero nova/premature-close/reconnect-failure oasis_events exist for any
   of the 20 sessions. The "reconnect:true" mark inside voice.latency.measured
   is a DELIBERATE code-driven context-upgrade reconnect (empty-context
   fast connect, then reconnect once real context resolves ~150-350ms
   later), not a failure path.
4. Remaining, unexplained: a ~5s gap between greeting_sent (on the
   upgraded, real-context connection) and audio_out_first_chunk, with zero
   instrumentation inside it. This VTID adds that instrumentation.

